From 809756dd282c359cc098964a08cdee336014476f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:51:21 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 10/48] Draw the save-data dialog and wait for the player's
 choice

The list modes (LISTLOAD, LISTSAVE, LISTDELETE) acted as if the player had
confirmed the first entry, and SAVE and DELETE went ahead without the
question a PSP asks: a list save overwrote the first listed save, a list
delete deleted the first one there was, all without anyone seeing it.

Those modes now open the port's save-data dialog over the running game
(host/ui/save_list_dialog.*): the game's slots with each save's title,
detail and date or "New data", then a Yes/No question (overwrite and delete
open on No); loading and deleting list only slots that hold a save. The
request stays VISIBLE until the player answers and the work is done then;
backing out reports result 1. The other modes are unchanged.

For tests and runs without a window, <prefix>_SAVEDATA_ANSWERS answers the
next asking requests in order (a save name, "new", "first" or "cancel").
<prefix>_SAVEDATA_INSTANT=1 skips the dialog as before but never
overwrites or deletes: a list load takes the first save, a list save the
first empty slot, a save goes ahead only over nothing, the rest cancel.

Verified on Windows (Vulkan, AMD) with a game's LISTSAVE of twenty slots
on an empty memory stick: listed, a slot chosen and confirmed with the
scripted virtual pad, saved, and the game went on. Not verified: LISTLOAD,
LISTDELETE, SAVE and DELETE with a game; the cancel result value (1) is
the common dialog's, not traced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
